# Lockfiles are tool-generated with LF. Pin them so line endings don't depend on
# a contributor's core.autocrlf setting (avoids spurious whole-file diffs).
*.lock text eol=lf

# The test suite's offline tiktoken cache (see packages/ci-core/conftest.py).
# tiktoken sha256-checks it, so it must reach disk byte for byte. It looks like
# text, and Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true would check it out with
# CRLF — which is exactly how litellm's own copy of this file broke in its
# Windows wheel. `binary` also keeps a 100,000-line diff out of every review.
packages/ci-core/tests/fixtures/tiktoken_cache/* binary

# A real Perplexity Agent API stream (2026-09-19), replayed by
# test_llm_perplexity_agent.py. Its bytes are the point: it is how the
# `"truncation": ""` that crashes litellm 1.96.2's route was found, and a stream
# built from the docs does not carry it. Byte for byte, like the cache above.
packages/ci-core/tests/fixtures/perplexity_agent/* binary
